      "file": "stator_magnetic_field.glb",
      "title": "Three phase currents make a rotating field",
      "description": "Three windings 120° apart carry currents 120° out of phase; their combined field rotates at synchronous speed n_s = 120·f / p (e.g. 1500 rpm for 4 poles at 50 Hz). The laminated core carries the flux with low eddy-current loss. Winding insulation (class F/H) is the life-limiting part: each ≈ 10 °C over its rating roughly halves insulation life, so overload, poor cooling and voltage unbalance matter. Test with insulation resistance / polarisation index.",
